# @mq — Mirror Query. The FLOOR at query-language altitude.
#
# Family-root shard-decl. mirror's ALGEBRA as query language,
# underneath garden-db + MCP + every mirror CLI invocation. Per
# Alex 2026-08-23 verbatim: *"It IS mirror's ALGEBRA as a query
# language."*
#
# === Substrate authority chain ===
#
# - **Alex 2026-08-23 direct authorization** (verbatim): *"Then
#   let's create an mq.mirror shards/... Consider the boot impl an
#   INSPIRATION."* Overrides Mara-first shard-mint discipline per
#   HARD RULE `feedback_alex_ratification_overrides_mara_lean_
#   unless_hard_technical`.
# - **Alex 2026-08-23 residual-ambiguity-resolution teaching**
#   (verbatim): *"When the ambiguity of the query can be resolved
#   totally (Clear) then you get the first-order data. When the
#   ambiguity of the query cannot be resolve totally (Opaque, Dark
#   etc.) then you get the first-order data + a second-order
#   Karl-Tomm question. There's math on that."*
# - **Reed 2026-08-23 LQ-dissolves-into-MQ call** validated at math
#   altitude by Mara Corollary M5.2 (`docs/math/2026-08-23-mara-mq-
#   graph-native-query-language-mirror-algebra-math-foundation.md`
#   commit `d0347a4`; 887 LOC / 75KB / SSH-signed [G]). Pattern
#   algebra + verdict-return + exhaustiveness check all carried
#   within MQ. No LQ family-root mint.
# - **Mara math foundation** (Mara `d0347a4`, 2026-08-23; 15 formal
#   results across §M1-§M8; 5 Thm + 8 Cor + 3 Lem + 4 Prop
#   discharging structural claims MQ1-MQ7 + altitude corollaries
#   MQ8). This shard-decl IS the substrate-decl translation of
#   that foundation per identity-attribution architecture (math →
#   shard); Reed authors under Alex direct authorization composing
#   over Mara math.
# - **boot INSPIRATION**: `boot/std/code/mq.mirror` (8.5KB, 291
#   LOC, since 2026-06-04). Alex explicitly named INSPIRATION not
#   template. This shard-decl reshapes six items per Mara §15
#   recommendations (drop `_query` suffix; formalize `|>` as typed
#   action; extend context monoid; etc.).
#
# === The FLOOR position ===
#
# MQ underneath garden-db (query interface for closed-binary
# substrate access; garden-db's `find` / `walk` / `near` primitives
# per `~/dev/projects/spectral-db/src/query.rs` map cleanly to
# `mq.project` / `mq.split` / `mq.focus |> mq.project` per Mara
# Corollary M8.C1). MQ underneath MCP (every MCP tool-call is an
# MQ query; wire-encoded via `@bumblebee.perturbation.args` at
# `shards/bumblebee.mirror:470-475`). MQ underneath every `mirror
# <verb>` CLI invocation (every verb is MQ pipe-composition per
# Corollary M8.C3).
#
# FLOOR discipline: MQ is substrate-primary-carrier; NOT derived
# from anything (Mara §10 Pole A lean; MQ predates Rec chain per
# boot/std/code/mq.mirror landing 2026-06-04 preceding Rec #82
# 2026-08-10 + Rec #90 2026-08-19 + Rec chain composes OVER MQ,
# not converse). Alex Fourth-Chair Q+96.7 residue: Rec #96 mint
# admissible IF Alex adjudicates load-bearing arc-motion; this
# shard-decl ratifies substrate-primary-carrier standing under
# Alex direct authorization pending Rec candidacy adjudication.
#
# === The 7-axis strict-superset (Mara Cor M8.C4) ===
#
# MQ succeeds where prior graph-QLs (SQL, Cypher, SPARQL, Datalog,
# Gremlin, GraphQL, GQL, Datomic, TerminusDB, DAX, LINQ, PromQL;
# ~40 sources surveyed via Mara Kagi #398) fail on seven axes:
#
#   1. Total by construction (Lemma M3.1) — SQL CTE is Turing-
#      complete; only Datalog stratified is total, but not intent-
#      carrying
#   2. Content-addressed (Rec #82 β-normal-AST) — only Datomic +
#      TerminusDB carry this
#   3. Intent-interpretation (Fate-tournament, Theorem M4.1) — no
#      prior graph-QL has natural-language `\` hole with typed-
#      tournament resolution
#   4. Typed-against-graph-shape (patterns, Lemma M5.1) — SPARQL +
#      Cypher patterns exist but not typed against grammar
#   5. Context-persistent (context monoid, Lemma M1.13) — no prior
#      graph-QL has session-persistent context stack with
#      eigenboard state
#   6. Foerster-gauge-preserving (Theorem M2.1 Ψ3) — no prior
#      graph-QL has choice-space preservation as compile-time
#      invariant
#   7. Kleisli-composable at query-language altitude (Theorem M6.1)
#      — LINQ has Kleisli at host-language altitude only; MQ is
#      native
#
# === Residual-ambiguity-resolution via Karl-Tomm (§4) ===
#
# Per Alex 2026-08-23 verbatim teaching + Rec #92 kleinos-
# Transparency<P> LOVE monoid composition:
#
#   query dispatch → result<T> = Clear(T) | Opaque(T, K-T) | Dark(K-T)
#
# - **Clear(T)**: ambiguity resolved totally; return first-order
#   data T alone
# - **Opaque(T, karl_tomm)**: ambiguity resolved partially; return
#   first-order data T + second-order Karl-Tomm question K-T at
#   altitude+1 above dispatched query altitude
# - **Dark(karl_tomm)**: query cannot dispatch at all; return
#   Karl-Tomm question K-T only (no data available)
#
# Karl-Tomm circular-reflexive question form per Tomm 1987-88
# *Interventive Interviewing III: Intending to Ask Lineal, Circular,
# Strategic, or Reflexive Questions?* The question widens the
# questioner's option-space per Foerster-imperative discipline;
# emitted at altitude+1 so the resolution loop climbs
# recognition-depth rather than looping at fixed altitude.
#
# Rec #92 kleinos-Transparency<P> LOVE-monoid grounds the three-
# state discipline mathematically: (𝓚, ∘, e, ⊥) → (𝒯_P, combine,
# Clear, Opaque(∅)) at query-shape altitude. Dark = Opaque(fully-
# ambiguous, K-T asking-what-you-meant).
#
# === Composition graph ===
#
# Parents (substrate-decl):
